---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="Markdown Syntax Reference — Everything SoloMD Supports"
  description="Every Markdown feature SoloMD supports: headings with auto-numbering, highlights, sub/superscripts, lists, code blocks, tables, KaTeX & LaTeX math, Mermaid diagrams, GitHub callouts, WikiLinks, tldraw whiteboards, and YAML front-matter."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container docs-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/docs/">Docs</a> / <span>Markdown Syntax</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>Markdown Syntax Reference</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        SoloMD supports CommonMark, GitHub Flavored Markdown (GFM), and rich writing extensions — all rendered in-place in Live Edit as well as in Split and Preview modes.
      </p>

      <h2>Headings &amp; Auto-Numbering</h2>
      <pre><code># H1
## H2
### H3
#### H4</code></pre>
      <p>
        <strong>Tip:</strong> Use <em>Paragraph → Auto-Number Headings (1 / 1.1 / 1.1.1)</em> for a one-shot numbering pass, or turn on <strong>“Automatically number 1–6 headings”</strong> in <em>Settings → General</em> so hierarchical numbers update automatically whenever headings are added, deleted, or moved.
      </p>

      <h2>Table of contents</h2>
      <pre><code>[TOC]</code></pre>
      <p>Put <code>[TOC]</code> on a line by itself to generate a linked, nested table of contents from the document headings.</p>

      <h2>Emphasis, Highlights &amp; Sub/Superscripts</h2>
      <pre><code>*italic* or _italic_
**bold** or __bold__
***bold italic***
~~strikethrough~~
==highlighted text== (Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + H)
`inline code`
H~2~O (subscript) and X^2^ (superscript)
&lt;u&gt;underline&lt;/u&gt; and &lt;kbd&gt;Ctrl+S&lt;/kbd&gt;</code></pre>

      <h2>Lists, Task Lists &amp; Indented Code Blocks</h2>
      <pre><code>- Unordered item
  - Nested item (Tab to indent, Shift+Tab to outdent)

1. First item (Enter continues with 2. and auto-renumbers)
2. Second item
   Press Shift+Enter for a soft break to insert an aligned code fence inside the list:
   ```python
   print("Preserves list indentation and auto-pads multi-line pastes")
   ```

- [x] Completed task
- [ ] Pending task #work 📅 2026-11-05 ⏫</code></pre>
      <p>
        <strong>Per-section numbering:</strong> ordered lists separated by headings, horizontal rules, code fences, or tables start fresh at <code>1.</code>, and typing <code>1.</code> manually starts a new numbering run.
      </p>

      <h2>WikiLinks, Links &amp; Images</h2>
      <pre><code>[[Another Note]]
[[folder/note|Custom Label]]
[External link](https://solomd.app "Tooltip")

![Alt text](./_assets/screenshot.png)</code></pre>
      <p>
        In Live Edit, hold <kbd>Ctrl</kbd> (<kbd>⌘</kbd> on macOS) and click a link to open it in your browser. Standalone images, images inside list items or blockquotes, linked images, and reference-style images all render in-place.
      </p>

      <h2>GitHub-style Callouts &amp; Blockquotes</h2>
      <pre><code>&gt; [!NOTE]
&gt; Supports NOTE, TIP, IMPORTANT, WARNING, and CAUTION callouts.

&gt; Regular blockquotes can also contain nested GFM tables in Live Edit and Preview.</code></pre>

      <h2>Code Blocks</h2>
      <pre><code>```rust
fn main() &#123;
    println!("Hello, SoloMD!");
&#125;
```</code></pre>
      <p>
        Typing <code>```</code> offers language autocomplete. Raw HTML tags (like <code>&lt;div&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;template&gt;</code>), math delimiters, and tables inside fenced code blocks stay completely inert. Pressing <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + A</kbd> once inside a code block selects only the code block body; pressing it a second time selects the whole document.
      </p>

      <h2>Tables</h2>
      <pre><code>| Left | Center | Right |
| :--- | :----: | ----: |
| a    | b      | c     |</code></pre>
      <p>
        Click any cell in Live Edit to place the caret directly inside that row and column. The floating table toolbar lets you add/remove rows and columns or type exact <code>Cols × Rows</code> dimensions. Pasting cells from Excel or WPS converts them automatically into a Markdown table.
      </p>

      <h2>Math (KaTeX — <code>$</code> and LaTeX <code>\(...\)</code>)</h2>
      <p>Inline: <code>$a^2 + b^2 = c^2$</code> or <code>\(a^2 + b^2 = c^2\)</code></p>
      <p>Block (supports <code>$$...$$</code> or <code>\[...\]</code>):</p>
      <pre><code>$$
\int_0^\infty e^&#123;-x^2&#125; \, dx = \frac&#123;\sqrt\pi&#125;&#123;2&#125;
$$</code></pre>

      <h2>Mermaid Diagrams, PlantUML &amp; tldraw Whiteboards</h2>
      <pre><code>```mermaid
flowchart LR
  A["Start (parentheses &amp; colons auto-quoted)"] --&gt; B&#123;Decision&#125;
  B --&gt;|Yes| C[Done]
```</code></pre>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mermaid v11:</strong> supports flowcharts, sequence, class, state, ER, gantt, pie, and mindmap diagrams, with automatic quoting for labels containing <code>@</code>, <code>()</code>, or <code>:</code>.</li>
        <li><strong>tldraw Whiteboards:</strong> insert a <code>```tldraw</code> block (or type <code>/whiteboard</code>) to embed an interactive drawing canvas stored directly inside your Markdown file.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Footnotes &amp; YAML Front-matter</h2>
      <pre><code>---
title: Weekly Notes
date: 2026-11-02
tags: [markdown, notes]
---

Here is a footnote reference[^1].

[^1]: Footnotes render cleanly and survive DOCX and PDF export.</code></pre>
    </article>
    <Giscus lang={lang} />
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>

<style>
  .docs-article { max-width: 820px; padding: 40px 20px 80px; }
  .breadcrumbs { font-size: 13px; color: var(--text-muted, #8a8a8a); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .breadcrumbs a { color: inherit; }
  .docs-article h1 { font-size: 2rem; margin: 10px 0 16px; }
  .docs-article h2 { font-size: 1.4rem; margin: 32px 0 12px; }
  .docs-article .lead { color: var(--text-muted, #555); margin-bottom: 24px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .docs-article code { background: #f5f5f0; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-size: 0.9em; }
  .docs-article pre { background: #f5f5f0; padding: 12px 16px; border-radius: 6px; overflow-x: auto; }
  .docs-article pre code { background: none; padding: 0; }
  .docs-article p, .docs-article li { line-height: 1.7; margin: 10px 0; }
</style>
